# Copy to `.env`. The real file is git-ignored and must stay that way.
#
# This is the development fallback, not the intended home for a credential. In
# ordinary use a provider key belongs in your operating system's credential
# store, put there by `codeflux provider set --name <provider>`, which reads it
# from standard input so it never reaches your shell history. Nothing in
# CodeFlux logs a key, returns one in an error, writes one to SQLite, or hands
# one to a worker process.

# Provider key. OPENAI_API_KEY wins when both are set, on the assumption that a
# machine with the specific name set has set it deliberately.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret settings overlay.
#
# Only the five CODEFLUX_* names below are accepted. Any other CODEFLUX_* key
# in the environment is a hard error rather than a silently ignored typo, so a
# misspelled setting cannot quietly leave you running the default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Provider endpoint override. A remote endpoint must also be explicitly
# approved; it is refused by default.
# CODEFLUX_PROVIDER_ENDPOINT=

# Hard budget. Exact integer minor units — 2500 with USD is $25.00. There is no
# floating point anywhere in a cost. Both names must be set together or
# neither: a limit without a currency is not a limit.
# CODEFLUX_HARD_BUDGET_MINOR=
# CODEFLUX_BUDGET_CURRENCY=

# Request timeout. A Go duration that must be a whole number of milliseconds.
# CODEFLUX_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=60s

# Policy preset.
# CODEFLUX_POLICY_PRESET=
